      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-10-10_WidnesExaminer_art0032" n="art0032">
        <head>COINVMD TO__TjlE POLTCE.STATION IN A</head>
        <p>COINVMD TO__TjlE POLTCE.STATION IN A</p>
        <p>WHEEL-BARROW.</p>
        <p>Walter Jerome, labourer, of 72, Liverpool-road, I Warrington was charged at the Borough Police Court on Monday with being helplessly drunk in front of the Town Hall on Sunday morning. Defendant was found by a police officer unable to walk at about 20 minutes to one o'clock on Sunday morning. He was compelled to borrow a wheel-barrow to take prisoner to the IPolice Station, Defendant, who seemed in the jovial ; mood, was fined Ss. 6d, and costs (55.) or seven days,</p>
        <p>-</p>
        <p>. - •</p>
      </div>
