        <p>STOCKTON HEATH. -- HILL CLIFFE AND STOCKTON HEATH UNITED BAND OF Horz.—There was a good attendance at the first public meeting of the session which was held in the Wesleyan schoolroom, Stockton Heath, on Monday evening, and the enthusiasm augured well for the session's work. Mr. Arthur Mounfield (president of the society) presided, and was accompanied on the platform by Rev. E. B. Keeling (Warrington) and Rev. J. S. Hughes (vice-president), and Mr. 61. Whitfield (secretary). A good programme was submitted and met with cordial approval. A pianoforte solo by Miss Lena Powell was much apprechtted. Miss Jones and Miss May Isherwood were heard to distinct advantage in their songs' whilst the duets contributed by Elsie Whitfield and Dolly Cain and the Misses Mom-field and L. Powell were much enjoyed. Recitations were supplied byßeggie Moss, Edward Phillips, Thomas Pearce, Albert Isherwood, Edith Cole, Emma Hamblett, Ada Mounfield, and Miss Townley. An action song "The child and the butterfly "given by 12 girls was applauded. Considerable amusement was caused by the humorous dialogue " Paddy's mistake " given by the adult members. During the evening Mr. B. Keeling delivered an interesting address. Mr. G. A. Whitfield played the pianoforte accompaniments.</p>
