        <p>Hockey. Latchford First Team last Saturday had Crewe Permanent Way as visitors and were defeated. The combination of the visiting forwards was good aud their goal-keeper played an exceptionally brilliant game. Banks and Scott scored for the home team, but Crewe nettedsfour times and proved to be the better team in a keen and pleasantly contested game. The Second Eleven journeyed to oppose New Brighton Wanderers" B " and won 3-1. The game I was not of a very thrilling description, the heat made things rather uncomfortable, but the home team did not last as well as the visitors. Booth, Starkey and Minards were the scorers for Latchford.</p>
